NoTooltip: No tooltip yet...
Name: Config Center
Name_ModConfig: Config Center(Beta Version)
ButtonApply: Apply Preset
ButtonInfo: More Info
ButtonDelete: Delete Preset
ButtonRename: Rename
ReadOnlyTip: You can only get the value of this option.

AboutPage: {
	Label: About
	Tooltip: About the new config interface.
	About:
		'''
		This is [c/0099ff:the brand new config interface] of Quality of Terraria, you will find all features here. Join our Discord server for feedback. It's totally okay to use the classic tModLoader mod config menu.

		At the left are the [c/0099ff:categories] based on functionality, click them to view their children entries.
		At the bottom is the [c/0099ff:tooltip], hover the cursor on an entry to view its tooltip.

		[c/0099ff:Right click] an entry to [c/0099ff:reset it to default].
		'''
	LinkDiscord: Discord: https://discord.gg/rEmGMQv5z7 (clickable!)
	LinkQQ: Hidden, only relavent for Chinese
}

AboutPage_ModConfig: {
	Label: About
	Tooltip: About the new config interface-Generalized.
	About:
		'''
		Please read the About of Quality of Terraria's [c/0099ff:the brand new config interface] first
		This is the extended version made by [c/9966cc:LogSpiral]
		So if you find some wierd bug when using [c/0099ff:config interface-Generalized], please inform that guy about the bug
		This basically contains the function of vanilla ModConfig. Use the vanilla version if you find some problem.

		The category cards cards are generated according to different configuration files within a mod by default
		and configuration options are generated by reflection of these configuration types by default

		The CustomConfigItem is not support currently.
		But an option will be devided to the most fundamental datas.

		The Bug We Known：
		1. Example mod -> ShowCaseA:DataTypes -> CustomKey may lead to a crash
		2. Set default value by right click may fail or crash when the option type is Color or others.

		It might be an document about how to make an custom-config page.

		Lastly, here's an [c/0099ff:cute Komeiji Koishi fumo] because LogSpiral likes her.
		'''
}

SingleConfigCategory.Tooltip:
	'''
	Configuration Interface Generated Based on Reflection
	In addition to the basic functionalities of the original configuration interface, new features have been added:
	-Colors now have a better setup interface. Whether HSL mode is enabled or not, 
	 both RGBA and HSL will be enabled simultaneously, and the hexadecimal code (Hex) can be edited.
	 Left-click on the color block to copy the hexadecimal code.
	 Right-click on the color block to paste.
	 Middle-click to toggle expansion.
	 The button next to the expand button will display the sliders in a more detailed and vibrant form.
	-Lists and other elements can now be resized by dragging the bottom edge.
	-Elements within lists and arrays can be dragged to reorder them.
	'''

Presets: {
	Label: Presets
	Tooltip: There are presets by Quality of Terraria for batch configuration. You may also create your own presets
	PlayerPresetTooltip: A player-defined preset
	DefaultPresetName: My Preset

	ExplorerPreset: {
		Label: "[centeritem:GravityGlobe] Explorer"
		Tooltip: Best for vanilla-like playthroughs. Explore while facing typical challenges with moderate assistance. Might work well with mods like Thorium or Spirit
		Link: https://github.com/ForOne-Club/ImproveGame/wiki/Config-Preset#explorer
	}

	WarriorPreset: {
		Label: "[centeritem:EmpressBlade] Fighter"
		Tooltip: Stop digging and start fighting! Skip most grindings. Might work well with mods like Calamity or Fargo's Souls
		Link: https://github.com/ForOne-Club/ImproveGame/wiki/Config-Preset#fighter
	}

	VanillaPreset: {
		Label: "[centeritem:MusicBoxCredits] Vanilla Enjoyer"
		Tooltip: Just like vanilla. Play with few QoL features
		Link: https://github.com/ForOne-Club/ImproveGame/wiki/Config-Preset#vanilla-enjoyer
	}

	AddPreset: {
		Label: "[centeritem:ImproveGame/AddIconDummy] Save as Preset"
		Tooltip: Saves the current config as a preset
		Link: https://github.com/ForOne-Club/ImproveGame/wiki/Config-Preset#adding-a-preset
	}

	OpenFolder: {
		Label: "[centeritem:ImproveGame/OpenFolderDummy] Open Preset Folder"
		Tooltip: Opens the preset folder
	}
}

Favorites: {
	Label: Favorited Entries
	Tooltip: <right> an entry to favorite it. Favorited entries will show up here
}

Everything: {
	Label: Everything
	Tooltip: All configurable features. You'll likely find searching to be useful
}

GameMechanics: {
	Label: Game Mechanics
	Tooltip: Edit game mechanics, e.g. Tombstone spawning & respawn speed
}

PylonMechanics: {
	Label: Pylon Mechanics
	Tooltip: Remove various pylon limitations
}

NpcSettings: {
	Label: Friendly NPCs
	Tooltip: Edit friendly NPC behaviors, e.g. housing & happiness
}

EnemySettings: {
	Label: Enemies
	Tooltip: Edit enemy behaviors, e.g. Lava Slime No Lava & coin drop rate
}

PlayerAbility: {
	Label: Player Abilities
	Tooltip: Boost player abilities, e.g. tile placement range, respawning with full heath, keep buffs on death & ore excavation
}

Multiplayer: {
	Label: Multiplayer
	Tooltip: Enhance multiplayer experience, e.g. auto-joining teams & unlimited teleportation
}

PlantSettings: {
	Label: Plants
	Tooltip: Edit plant behaviors, e.g. herb growth speed, tree heights & gem tree drops
}

ItemSettings: {
	Label: Items
	Tooltip: Edit item behaviors, which can save grinding, e.g. infinite ammo/potions & buff stations from inventory
}

ModItemSettings: {
	Label: Mod Items
	Tooltip: Here you can modify some of the settings for Quality of Terraria items, and adjust whether some items are obtainable.
}

VisualAndInterface: {
	Label: Visuals
	Tooltip: Edit vanilla & QoT visuals, tweak QoT user interfaces
}

ModFeatures: {
	Label: Others
	Tooltip: Edit other features, e.g. Ammo Chain, Auto-trash & Big backpack
}

Minimap: {
	Label: Map
	Tooltip: Edit map features, e.g. Locators
}

Keybinds: {
	Label: Controls
	Tooltip: Manage Quality of Terraria hotkeys, <right> on an entry to set it to default
	// 快捷键会在Tooltip显示其默认绑定的键位
	Default: Default: {0}
}
